{"name":"Sophomore","hex":"#7d7170","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sophomore","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["The second in a series, especially, the second of an artist’s albums or the second of four years in a high school (tenth grade) or university.","Sophomoric."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A second-year undergraduate student in a college or university, or a second-year student in a four-year secondary school or high school.","A three-year-old horse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophomore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sophomore","blocks":[{"text":"In the United States, a sophomore is a person in the second year at an educational institution; usually at a secondary school or at the college and university level, but also in other forms of post-secondary educational institutions or even primary schools. In high school, a sophomore is equivalent to a tenth grade or Class-10 student."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/1920_Locust_yearbook_p._085_%28Sophomore%29.jpg/330px-1920_Locust_yearbook_p._085_%28Sophomore%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophomore","wikidata":"Q97360440"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/%22Pass_in_Review%22_Riverside_Military_Academy_yearbook%2C_Part_1%2C_Gainesville%2C_Georgia%2C_1911_-_DPLA_-_fd0109a1565cc8789c26908e1c71b0f7.pdf/page58-500px-%22Pass_in_Review%22_Riverside_Military_Academy_yearbook%2C_Part_1%2C_Gainesville%2C_Georgia%2C_1911_-_DPLA_-_fd0109a1565cc8789c26908e1c71b0f7.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/%22Pass_in_Review%22_Riverside_Military_Academy_yearbook%2C_Part_1%2C_Gainesville%2C_Georgia%2C_1911_-_DPLA_-_fd0109a1565cc8789c26908e1c71b0f7.pdf/page58-1280px-%22Pass_in_Review%22_Riverside_Military_Acade